# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-cad-denotation-picks-dwg-trueview — --cad accoreconsole selects DWG TrueView's accoreconsole
#+STATUS: DONE (alfe 2.2.81, 2026-09-24)
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: claude/dreamy-ptolemy-uj8mzd

* Symptom

Reported by pjb on the Windows host PF5S26BT, which has both AutoCAD 2022
and the free DWG TrueView 2024 viewer (French) installed:

#+begin_example
$ alfe --list-cad-programs
acad-2022                C:/Program Files/Autodesk/AutoCAD 2022/acad.exe
accoreconsole-2022       C:/Program Files/Autodesk/AutoCAD 2022/accoreconsole.exe
accoreconsole-2024       C:/Program Files/Autodesk/DWG TrueView 2024 - French/accoreconsole.exe
bricscad-v25-fr_FR       C:/Program Files/Bricsys/BricsCAD V25 fr_FR/bricscad.exe
clautolisp               (embedded in alfe)
#+end_example

Selecting accoreconsole ran the TrueView one, which aborts at bootstrap:

#+begin_example
alfe: alfe AUTOCAD backend error (phase BOOTSTRAP): AutoCAD process exited
before READY (exit 1): ...
Execution Path:
C:\Program Files\Autodesk\DWG TrueView 2024 - French\accoreconsole.exe
...
Le fichier de configuration a peut-être été verrouillé par un autre
processus ou défini en lecture seule (.cfg, .bak). Fichier: C:\Program
Files\Autodesk\DWG TrueView 2024 - French\dwgviewr2024.cfg
...
ERREUR FATALE:  Impossible de traiter le fichier de configuration !
#+end_example

* Cause

Two discovery paths exist. =discover-accoreconsole-binary= (plain
=--autocad=) already ranks TrueView last (=%accoreconsole-preference=,
alfe-cad-console-encoding.issue). But =discover-cad-programs= — behind
=--list-cad-programs= and =--cad= — denoted TrueView's executable
=accoreconsole-2024=, and =resolve-cad-denotation= picks the *latest*
version among matches, so =--cad accoreconsole= and =--cad autocad --mode
batch= chose TrueView 2024 over AutoCAD 2022.

DWG TrueView is not AutoCAD: a read-only viewer that cannot create or
modify entities, whose configuration file lives in Program Files (so it
aborts for a normal user).

* Resolution (alfe 2.2.81)

The TrueView accoreconsole is now a distinct product in the listing, with
its own denotation =dwgtrueview-YYYY= (=%dwg-trueview-path-p= in
=backend-cad-common.lisp=). =accoreconsole[-YYYY]= and =autocad[-YYYY]=
never match it; it remains selectable explicitly with =--cad dwgtrueview=.
Regression tests: =cad-program-denotation-parsing= and
=cad-denotation-resolution= (=autolisp-front-end/tests/backend-cad-tests.lisp=).
